prompt --application/shared_components/user_interface/templates/region/form_progress
begin
wwv_flow_imp_shared.create_plug_template(
 p_id=>wwv_flow_imp.id(754593078725477918)
,p_layout=>'TABLE'
,p_template=>wwv_flow_string.join(wwv_flow_t_varchar2(
'<section class="amc-TFormProgress #REGION_CSS_CLASSES#" id="#REGION_STATIC_ID#" #REGION_ATTRIBUTES# aria-labelledby="#REGION_STATIC_ID#_heading" data-amc-label-count="%0 of %1 required fields done" data-amc-label-done="All %0 required fields done" data-amc-label-next="Next: %0" data-amc-label-draft="Save a draft now and finish the rest later." data-amc-label-optional="Optional" data-amc-label-filled="filled" data-amc-label-empty="still empty" data-amc-required-marker="Value Required">',
'  <div class="amc-TFormProgress-surface">',
'    <div class="amc-TFormProgress-head">',
'      <div class="amc-TFormProgress-meter" aria-hidden="true" hidden></div>',
'      <header class="amc-TFormProgress-header">',
'        <span class="amc-TFormProgress-icon fa #ICON_CSS_CLASSES#" aria-hidden="true"></span>',
'        <h2 class="amc-TFormProgress-title" id="#REGION_STATIC_ID#_heading">#TITLE#</h2>',
'        <div class="amc-TFormProgress-status" hidden>',
'          <p class="amc-TFormProgress-count"><span class="amc-TFormProgress-check fa fa-check" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="amc-TFormProgress-countText"></span></p>',
'          <button type="button" class="amc-TFormProgress-next"></button>',
'        </div>',
'        <div class="amc-TFormProgress-actions">#HELP##EDIT##CHANGE##COPY##DELETE##CREATE#</div>',
'      </header>',
'      <p class="amc-TFormProgress-draft" hidden></p>',
'    </div>',
'    <div class="amc-TFormProgress-body">#BODY##SUB_REGIONS#</div>',
'    <footer class="amc-TFormProgress-footer">#PREVIOUS##CLOSE##NEXT#</footer>',
'    <p class="amc-TFormProgress-live" role="status" aria-live="polite"></p>',
'  </div>',
'</section>'))
,p_page_plug_template_name=>'AMC Form Progress'
,p_internal_name=>'AMC_TPL_FORM_PROGRESS'
,p_javascript_file_urls=>'#APP_FILES#amc-templates/amc-tpl-form-progress.js'
,p_css_file_urls=>'#APP_FILES#amc-templates/amc-tpl-form-progress.css'
,p_theme_id=>42
,p_default_label_alignment=>'RIGHT'
,p_default_field_alignment=>'LEFT'
,p_translate_this_template=>'N'
,p_template_comment=>'Living region template for forms. Design principles: Zeigarnik effect, used honestly: an open task stays in mind, so the frame shows a finite, visible distance to completion; only required items count and nothing is faked, so the meter never promises more than the form asks. Form design: the next empty required field is one click away, and with the Mark optional fields option the optional items are labelled instead of the required ones. How it works: the script finds the items in the region body by Universal Theme markup and treats an item as required when its field container has is-required, its control has required or aria-required="true", or its label carries a required marker: a visually hidden text containing (Value Required), a .t-Form-required element or a trailing asterisk. Hidden, disabled and conditionally not rendered items do not count. An item is filled when apex.item(id).isEmpty() is false, or, without the API, when its control has a value or a checked option. The header shows "4 of 7 required fields done" and a Next button naming the next empty required item after the focused one; a click on a meter segment focuses that item. When the last one is filled the segments turn to the success color one after another and the text reads "All 7 required fields done". The count is announced politely through a status region after each completed edit (change or leaving a field), never on every keystroke. It recalculates after apexafterrefresh, when Dynamic Actions show or hide items, and when values change. Forms with more than 24 required items get a continuous bar. English strings to translate, on the section element in the template or per region as Custom Attributes: data-amc-label-count %0 of %1 required fields done, data-amc-label-done All %0 required fields done, data-amc-label-next Next: %0, data-amc-label-draft Save a draft now and finish the rest later., data-amc-label-optional Optional, data-amc-label-filled filled, data-amc-label-empty still empty, data-amc-required-marker Value Required (the text of the hidden required marker in your language). Keyboard: the Next button is a real button in the header; segments are a pointer shortcut and hidden from assistive technology because the count and the button carry the same information. Reduced motion: no color sweep or transitions. Forced colors: segments use Highlight. JavaScript API: amcTplFormProgress.refresh(element) and result(element) returning total, done and the items.'
);
end;
/
